nt :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186411114}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "31ca1a18-e271-54de-8d6a-f0aa14857b82" :question/math-academy-id "q-182517" :question/problem "Find the missing values in the following truth table:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-1}} |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | {{field-3}} |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\n \n\nUsing your results, complete the following statement:\n\n$$\n(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B){{field-4}}A\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's solve for the missing values:\n\n- When $A≡\\text{T}$ and $B≡\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B) & ≡(\\text{T}∧\\text{T})∨¬(\\text{T}∨¬\\text{T}) \\\\  & ≡(\\text{T}∧\\text{T})∨¬(\\text{T}∨\\text{F}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}∨¬\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $A≡\\text{T}$ and $B≡\\text{F},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B) & ≡(\\text{T}∧\\text{F})∨¬(\\text{T}∨¬\\text{F}) \\\\  & ≡(\\text{T}∧\\text{F})∨¬(\\text{T}∨\\text{T}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}∨¬\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}∨\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- When $A≡\\text{F}$ and $B≡\\text{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B) & ≡(\\text{F}∧\\text{T})∨¬(\\text{F}∨¬\\text{T}) \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}∨¬\\text{F} \\\\  & ≡\\text{F}∨\\text{T} \\\\  & ≡\\text{T}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur completed table is shown below.\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B)\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n\nTo determine whether $(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B)$ is logically equivalent to $A,$ we need to check whether their truth tables are equivalent.\n\nWe see that the columns for $(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B)$ and $A$ are different. They differ in the second and third rows. Therefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\n(A∧B)∨¬(A∨¬B)≢A.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157794 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157231 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc5b8688-3838-5e9e-9304-9a4c787034ee" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Logically Equivalent Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d9123f6-1ac3-577d-8448-fa5f35090fb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477461} {:answer/id #uuid "7f5ec496-8711-51ea-967c-940ed57f12cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477462}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f5ec496-8711-51ea-967c-940ed57f12cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477462} :answer-field/id #uuid "a41e8230-3016-56f5-9ecd-0c0ca53982c9" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477700} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b9f76af-3775-5573-8674-5ed519df7677" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477463} {:answer/id #uuid "c3b32afa-ec9b-50ed-9315-54748539b4b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477464}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3b32afa-ec9b-50ed-9315-54748539b4b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477464} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9bb9216-5611-5306-b6e2-7e2dbeb9f076" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477701} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d2422dd1-c3e9-5d60-8594-d85ecf4d1266" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477465} {:answer/id #uuid "2d788219-eebe-5d12-9e1f-57b8008ed228" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477466}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2422dd1-c3e9-5d60-8594-d85ecf4d1266" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477465} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebb1ad31-5edb-5c7d-ae51-d6dab75641d2" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477702}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7074b983-3ace-5190-bf87-4742f8c8239b" :question/math-academy-id "q-81053" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are logically equivalent?\n- **I.** $¬A∧B$\n- **II.** $¬(A∨¬B)$\n- **III.** $A∨¬B$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Two statements are logically equivalent if they have the same truth table. So, we construct a truth table for the three given statements:\n\n| $\\,A\\,$ | $\\,B\\,$ | $\\,¬A∧B\\,$ | $\\,¬(A∨¬B)\\,$ | $\\,A∨¬B\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{T}$ | $\\text{F}$ |\n| $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{F}$ | $\\text{T}$ |\n\nWe see that only the statements $¬A∧B$ and $¬(A∨¬B)$ have the same truth table, so they are logically equivalent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377784 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #